<title>UK: Tate &amp; Lyle off amid losses in food sector.</title>
<headline>Tate &amp; Lyle off amid losses in food sector.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in food manufacturer Tate &amp; Lyle fell, tracking losses in leading British food retailers' shares after brokerage ABN AMRO Hoare Govett reiterated its view that the sector was overvalued, traders said.</p>
<p>By 1156 GMT, the shares were down 10-1/2p to 450p, a nine-month low.</p>
<p>Analysts at ABN AMRO Hoare Govett were not available to comment.</p>
<p>--Debra Sherman, London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
</text>
